  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Maximum height is achieved when the projection is along the vertical direction,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>136</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p>Now, for maximum range, angle of projection should be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mn>136</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>272</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p>"
  }
